# Power Chords: Open Riff (repertoire plan: st-power-chords-open). An original riff in E minor.
# Every chord is an eighth-note downstroke. Open shapes: E5 (022xxx), A5 (x022xx), D5 (xx023x);
# movable shapes: G5 (355xxx) and C5 (x355xx). Bars 1, 3 and 5 are the hook on E5 (hit, hit,
# rest, hit, hit, rest, hit, rest); the bars between answer it, and every jump between an open
# shape and a movable one has a rest in front of it. It ends D5 to a ringing E5 (bVII to i).
# Fingers: E5 and A5 with 2 and 3 (as in the E and Am chords), D5 with 1 and 3 (as in D),
# G5 and C5 with 1, 3 and 4.
title: Power Chords: Open Riff
